Kind: ablation
Issue: #786
Takes out: fpu_area_set_legacy()'s marking of x87 and SSE in XSTATE_BV -- a thread that has never used SSE is restored with them initial, and act_test's arm twenty-three's thread finds XMM0 zero rather than what was written
Accel: kvm
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 4
Note: KVM only, a true property and not a flake -- the defect is XRSTOR loading the initial XMM registers when XSTATE_BV[1] is clear (SDM Vol. 1, 253665-093US, Sec. 13.8), and TCG's XRSTOR loads the legacy region regardless, so on TCG the written XMM0 comes back whether the marking is there or not and nothing can see the defect.  Caught 2 of 2 KVM boots on OMEGA, missed 2 of 2 TCG boots, which is this line.
Expect: act_test: \[23\] .* and the thread found XMM0 0x0{32} and MXCSR

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/thread/fpu.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/thread/fpu.c
index 6d49afbf..d354946c 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/thread/fpu.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/thread/fpu.c
@@ -527,9 +527,8 @@ int fpu_area_set_legacy(void *area, const uint8_t *image)
 		uint64_t *bv = (uint64_t *)(dst + XSTATE_BV_OFFSET);
 		uint64_t *comp = (uint64_t *)(dst + XCOMP_BV_OFFSET);
 
-		*bv |= XCR0_X87 | XCR0_SSE;
-		if (*comp & XCOMP_BV_COMPACTED)
-			*comp |= XCR0_X87 | XCR0_SSE;
+		(void) bv;
+		(void) comp;
 	}
 	return 1;
 }
